In the discussion, James provided a detailed overview of a case study on the fiscal benefits of investing in Integrated Water Resources Management (IWRM) to mitigate flood risk in Nigeria, highlighting the severe economic impacts of flooding, including losses exceeding US$9 billion. I explained that IWRM offers a fiscally efficient solution, with benefit-cost ratios around 4:1, and discussed various strategies and real-world implementations in Nigeria, emphasizing the importance of effective governance and planning. We concluded with a tailored one-sentence summary, emphasizing IWRM's potential to deliver significant returns and protection for public budgets, aimed at international ministries of finance.
